-- Tests for body-a: Penal Code 1871 Chapter 16, ss 299-358
-- (pc-body-a-life.l4, pc-body-a-hurt.l4, pc-body-a-force.l4).
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: each Illustration is cited on the line
-- above its assertion (`-- s 350 illus (a)`); boundary cases for every age,
-- duration and count are on the helpers, both sides of the line. A failing
-- assertion here is a finding, not a typo: never edit an expected value to
-- make it pass.
--
-- Fixtures are full record literals, every field spelled; a leaf the facts
-- do not make TRUE is FALSE, as the charge generator's schema completion would
-- make it. (They were expanded from a compact spec by a script that checks
-- every field name against the DECLAREs, so a misspelt leaf cannot silently
-- default.)

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-hurt`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-force`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-life`

§ `body-a tests`

`the particulars` MEANS Particulars WITH
    accused            IS "A"
    date               IS "the 1st day of January 2026"
    time               IS ""
    place              IS "Orchard Road"
    `co-accused`       IS ""
    `common intention` IS FALSE

§§ `The threshold helpers - both sides of each line`

-- s 320(h): "during the space of 20 days"
#ASSERT `lasts the space of 20 days` 20
#ASSERT NOT `lasts the space of 20 days` 19
-- ss 354(2), 354A(2)(b): "below 14 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 14 years of age` 13
#ASSERT NOT `below 14 years of age` 14
-- s 300 Exception 5: "above 18 years of age" (completed years; F-10)
#ASSERT `above 18 years of age` 18
#ASSERT NOT `above 18 years of age` 17
-- s 300 Exception 6: "below 12 months of age"
#ASSERT `below 12 months of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 months of age` 12
-- s 305(2): "minor" - "below 18 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 18 years of age` 17
#ASSERT NOT `below 18 years of age` 18
-- s 312: "more than 16 weeks' duration"
#ASSERT `more than 16 weeks' duration` 17
#ASSERT NOT `more than 16 weeks' duration` 16
-- s 317: "below 12 years of age"
#ASSERT `below 12 years of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 years of age` 12

§§ `Hurt - ss 319-335`

-- s 319 Explanation: causing another to be unconscious is causing hurt.
%%FIXTURE A knocks Z unconscious
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by striking the said Z on the head with his fist
true: caused the victim to be unconscious; intention of causing hurt
%%END
#ASSERT `causes hurt` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT `voluntarily causes hurt` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT `offence under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`
#ASSERT NOT (`grievous hurt within section 320` `A knocks Z unconscious`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause hurt to one Z, to wit, by striking the said Z on the head with his fist, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 323 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A knocks Z unconscious`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"

-- A refusal: the blow causes nothing. s 321 needs hurt in fact.
%%FIXTURE A swings at Z and misses
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by swinging his fist at the said Z
true: intention of causing hurt
%%END
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 323` `A swings at Z and misses`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A swings at Z and misses`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323` `A swings at Z and misses`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 323 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of voluntarily causing hurt (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: does thereby cause hurt (bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness - s 319) to any person; the elements of section 321 taken together."

-- s 322 illus: A, intending or knowing himself likely permanently to
-- disfigure Z's face, gives Z a blow which does not disfigure but causes
-- severe bodily pain for 20 days. A has voluntarily caused grievous hurt.
%%FIXTURE s 322 illus
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by giving the said Z a blow to the face
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt; the hurt caused the sufferer to be in severe bodily pain during the space of 20 days
%%END
-- s 322 illus
#ASSERT `voluntarily causes grievous hurt` `s 322 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 325` `s 322 illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 323A` `s 322 illus`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 325` `s 322 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause grievous hurt to one Z, to wit, by giving the said Z a blow to the face, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 325 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 322 Explanation: grievous hurt caused but not intended or foreseen is not
-- "voluntarily causing grievous hurt".
%%FIXTURE s 322 Explanation, grievous hurt not intended
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by pushing the said Z
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone
%%END
#ASSERT `grievous hurt within section 320` `s 322 Explanation, grievous hurt not intended`
#ASSERT NOT (`voluntarily causes grievous hurt` `s 322 Explanation, grievous hurt not intended`)

-- s 323A illus: the punch at the club, intending minor injuries; Z falls,
-- hits his head and is permanently paralysed.
%%FIXTURE s 323A illus
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by punching the said Z in the face once, causing the said Z to lose his balance, to fall and to hit his head against a ledge, resulting in the said Z suffering severe brain injuries and being permanently paralysed
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous; the hurt caused is destruction or permanent impairing of the powers of any member or joint; the hurt caused endangers life
%%END
-- s 323A illus
#ASSERT `offence under s 323A` `s 323A illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 323` `s 323A illus`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 325` `s 323A illus`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 323A` `s 323A illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause hurt with the intention to cause hurt which is not grievous, but which actually caused grievous hurt to one Z, to wit, by punching the said Z in the face once, causing the said Z to lose his balance, to fall and to hit his head against a ledge, resulting in the said Z suffering severe brain injuries and being permanently paralysed, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 323A of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 324: a stab with a knife, hurt not grievous.
%%FIXTURE A cuts Z with a knife
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by slashing the said Z's forearm with a knife
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 324` `A cuts Z with a knife`
#ASSERT `offence under s 323` `A cuts Z with a knife`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 324` `A cuts Z with a knife`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause hurt to one Z by means of an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, to wit, by slashing the said Z's forearm with a knife, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 324 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 326: the same knife, grievous hurt intended and caused.
%%FIXTURE A stabs Z and fractures a rib
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by stabbing the said Z in the chest with a knife
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt; the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone; by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 326` `A stabs Z and fractures a rib`
#ASSERT `offence under s 325` `A stabs Z and fractures a rib`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 326` `A stabs Z and fractures a rib`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to caning or if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, liable to fine"

-- s 327: hurt to make Z hand over his wallet.
%%FIXTURE A beats Z for his wallet
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by punching the said Z until he handed over his wallet
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any property or valuable security
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 327` `A beats Z for his wallet`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 330` `A beats Z for his wallet`)

-- s 328: a drink drugged to facilitate an offence; no hurt need follow.
%%FIXTURE A drugs Z's drink
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by adding a sedative to the said Z's drink
true: administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood; with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 328` `A drugs Z's drink`
#ASSERT NOT (`voluntarily causes hurt` `A drugs Z's drink`)

-- s 330 illus (a): A, a police officer, tortures Z to make him confess.
-- illus (b): tortures B to point out where stolen property is (restoration).
-- illus (c): a customs officer tortures Z to confess a pretended offence.
%%FIXTURE s 330 illus (a)
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by beating the said Z
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct
%%END
%%FIXTURE s 330 illus (b)
type: Hurt Facts
victim: B
the manner: by beating the said B
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security
%%END
-- s 330 illus (a)
#ASSERT `offence under s 330` `s 330 illus (a)`
-- s 330 illus (b)
#ASSERT `offence under s 330` `s 330 illus (b)`
-- s 330 illus (c) is illus (a) on its atoms: the confession is to a
-- pretended offence, which the purpose leaf does not distinguish.
#ASSERT `offence under s 330` `s 330 illus (a)`

-- s 332: hurt to a police officer making an arrest.
%%FIXTURE A punches a police officer
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Sergeant Tan
victim described as: a police officer
the manner: by punching the said Sergeant Tan on the chest
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the sufferer is a public servant; in the discharge of his duty as such public servant
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 332` `A punches a police officer`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 332` `A punches a police officer`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did voluntarily cause hurt to one Sergeant Tan, a police officer, a public servant, in the discharge of his duty as such public servant, to wit, by punching the said Sergeant Tan on the chest, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 332 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 334: hurt on grave and sudden provocation, provisos met: s 334, not s 323.
%%FIXTURE A slaps Z on provocation
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by slapping the said Z
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; on grave and sudden provocation; neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation; the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person; the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers; the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 334` `A slaps Z on provocation`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 323` `A slaps Z on provocation`)

-- s 335 Explanation, applying s 300 Exception 1 proviso (b) (cf s 300 illus
-- (c)): provocation by a lawful arrest does not mitigate - s 323, not s 334.
%%FIXTURE A slaps the arresting officer
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by slapping the said Z
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; on grave and sudden provocation; neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation; the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person; the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence
%%END
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 334` `A slaps the arresting officer`)
#ASSERT `offence under s 323` `A slaps the arresting officer`

-- s 335: grievous hurt on provocation - s 335, and s 325 withdraws.
%%FIXTURE A breaks Z's arm on provocation
type: Hurt Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by twisting the said Z's arm until it broke
true: caused bodily pain; intention of causing hurt; the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt; the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone; on grave and sudden provocation; neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation; the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person; the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers; the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 335` `A breaks Z's arm on provocation`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 325` `A breaks Z's arm on provocation`)

§§ `Rash and negligent acts - ss 304A, 335B-338`

%%FIXTURE A drives rashly and injures Z
type: Rash Act Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by driving motor car SBA1234A through a red light at the junction of Orchard Road and Scotts Road and colliding with the said Z
true: does the act rashly; so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others; causes hurt to any person
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 337(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
-- s 26F(2): a rash act also makes out the negligent limb.
#ASSERT `offence under s 337(b)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
#ASSERT `offence under s 336(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 338(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 337(a)` `A drives rashly and injures Z`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did cause hurt to one Z by doing an act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others, to wit, by driving motor car SBA1234A through a red light at the junction of Orchard Road and Scotts Road and colliding with the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 337(a) of the Penal Code 1871."

%%FIXTURE A drives negligently and kills Z
type: Rash Act Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by failing to keep a proper lookout while reversing lorry YM1234B and colliding with the said Z
true: does the act negligently; so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others; causes the death of any person; not amounting to culpable homicide
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 304A(b)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 304A(a)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304A(b)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did cause the death of one Z by doing a negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide, to wit, by failing to keep a proper lookout while reversing lorry YM1234B and colliding with the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304A(b) of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304A(a)` `A drives negligently and kills Z`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 304A(a) would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of causing death by rash act (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: by doing a rash act."

%%FIXTURE A drops a brick from a block knowing it may kill
type: Rash Act Facts
the manner: by throwing a brick from the 20th storey of Block 1 onto a walkway
true: so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others; knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 335B` `A drops a brick from a block knowing it may kill`

§§ `Wrongful restraint and confinement - ss 339-348`

-- s 339 illus: A obstructs a path along which Z has a right to pass, A not
-- believing in good faith that he has a right to stop the path. Z is thereby
-- prevented from passing. A wrongfully restrains Z.
%%FIXTURE s 339 illus
type: Restraint Facts
victim: Z
true: voluntarily obstructs that person; so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction; in which that person has a right to proceed
%%END
-- s 339 illus
#ASSERT `wrongfully restrains` `s 339 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 341` `s 339 illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`wrongfully confines` `s 339 illus`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 341` `s 339 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did wrongfully restrain one Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 341 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- s 339 Exception: the same obstruction of a private way which A believes in
-- good faith he has a lawful right to obstruct is not an offence.
%%FIXTURE s 339 Exception
type: Restraint Facts
victim: Z
true: voluntarily obstructs that person; so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction; in which that person has a right to proceed; the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which he in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct
%%END
-- s 339 Exception
#ASSERT NOT (`wrongfully restrains` `s 339 Exception`)

-- s 340 illus (a): A causes Z to go within a walled space, and locks Z in.
-- illus (b): A places men with firearms at the outlets of a building and
-- tells Z they will fire if Z attempts to leave. A wrongfully confines Z.
%%FIXTURE s 340 illus (a)
type: Restraint Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by locking the said Z in a walled compound
true: voluntarily obstructs that person; so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction; in which that person has a right to proceed; in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits
%%END
-- s 340 illus (a)
#ASSERT `wrongfully confines` `s 340 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 342` `s 340 illus (a)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 342` `s 340 illus (a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did wrongfully confine one Z, to wit, by locking the said Z in a walled compound, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 342 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 340 illus (b) is illus (a) on the same atoms: the obstruction by threat of
-- firearms is `voluntarily obstructs that person` (its @desc says so).
#ASSERT `wrongfully confines` `s 340 illus (a)`

-- s 347: confined for ransom.
%%FIXTURE A confines Z for ransom
type: Restraint Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by keeping the said Z in a locked room until his family paid $50,000
true: voluntarily obstructs that person; so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction; in which that person has a right to proceed; in such a manner as to prevent that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits; for the purpose of extorting from the person confined, or from any person interested in him, any property or valuable security
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 347` `A confines Z for ransom`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 348` `A confines Z for ransom`)

§§ `Criminal force and assault - ss 349-358`

-- s 350 illus (a): A unfastens the moorings of Z's boat, which drifts. A has
-- intentionally used force to Z (by disposing substances); if without Z's
-- consent and intending injury, fear or annoyance, criminal force.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (a)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by disposing any substance so that the motion takes place without any further act; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
-- s 350 illus (a)
#ASSERT `uses force` `s 350 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (a)`

-- s 350 illus (b): A lashes Z's horse, which quickens its pace: change of
-- motion to Z by inducing an animal.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (b)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by inducing any animal to move, to change its motion, or to cease to move; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
-- s 350 illus (b)
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (b)`

-- s 350 illus (c): A, intending to cause hurt to Z, seizes Z's horse and stops
-- it: cessation of motion by his own bodily power, in order to commit an
-- offence.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (c)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by his own bodily power; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; in order to cause the committing of any offence
%%END
-- s 350 illus (c)
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (c)`

-- s 350 illus (d): A intentionally pushes against Z in the street.
-- illus (f): A intentionally pulls up a woman's veil. Both are own bodily
-- power, causing motion or contact; criminal force if without consent and
-- intending or knowing likely injury, fear or annoyance.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (d)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by his own bodily power; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
-- s 350 illus (d)
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (d)`

-- s 350 illus (e) and (g): a thrown stone, and boiling water poured into a
-- bath - a substance brought into contact with Z or his clothes, by A's own
-- bodily power.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (e)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes to any substance such motion as brings that substance into contact with that other's body, or with anything he is wearing or carrying, or so situated that the contact affects his sense of feeling; by his own bodily power; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
-- s 350 illus (e)
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (e)`

-- s 350 illus (h): A incites a dog to spring upon Z, without Z's consent,
-- intending injury, fear or annoyance.
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (h)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by inducing any animal to move, to change its motion, or to cease to move; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
-- s 350 illus (h)
#ASSERT `uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (h)`

-- s 350: force used WITH consent is not criminal force (illus (a)'s "if ...
-- without Z's consent").
%%FIXTURE s 350 illus (a), with consent
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by disposing any substance so that the motion takes place without any further act; intentionally uses force; intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person
%%END
#ASSERT `uses force` `s 350 illus (a), with consent`
#ASSERT NOT (`uses criminal force` `s 350 illus (a), with consent`)

-- s 351 illus (a): A shakes his fist at Z, intending or knowing it likely
-- that Z will believe A is about to strike him. illus (b): A begins to unloose
-- the muzzle of a ferocious dog. A has committed an assault.
%%FIXTURE s 351 illus (a)
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by shaking his fist at the said Z
true: makes any gesture or any preparation; intending or knowing it to be likely that it will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person
%%END
-- s 351 illus (a) and (b)
#ASSERT `commits an assault` `s 351 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 352` `s 351 illus (a)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 352` `s 351 illus (a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did assault one Z, to wit, by shaking his fist at the said Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 352 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 351 Explanation: mere words do not amount to an assault - no gesture or
-- preparation, no assault.
%%FIXTURE s 351 Explanation, mere words
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
true: intending or knowing it to be likely that it will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person
%%END
#ASSERT NOT (`commits an assault` `s 351 Explanation, mere words`)

-- s 354(1): an outrage of modesty, charged as text.
%%FIXTURE A touches Z's breast
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by touching the said Z's breast
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by his own bodily power; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury, fear or annoyance to that person; intending to outrage the modesty of that person
%%END
#ASSERT `offence under s 354(1)` `A touches Z's breast`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 354(2)` `A touches Z's breast`)
#ASSERT `offence under s 352` `A touches Z's breast`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 354(1)` `A touches Z's breast`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of January 2026, at Orchard Road, Singapore, did use criminal force to one Z, intending to outrage the modesty of the said person, to wit, by touching the said Z's breast, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 354(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 354(2)` `A touches Z's breast`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 354(2) would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of assault or use of criminal force to a person below 14 years of age with intent to outrage modesty (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: against any person below 14 years of age."

-- s 354(2) and s 354A(2)(b): the victim is below 14. The s 350 purpose is
-- "in order to cause the committing of any offence" - the s 354 offence itself
-- (body-a-forks.md F-8).
%%FIXTURE A molests a child of 13 in a lift, restraining her
type: Criminal Force Facts
victim: Z
the manner: by pinning the said Z against the wall of the lift and touching her breast
true: causes motion, change of motion, or cessation of motion to that other; by his own bodily power; intentionally uses force; without that person's consent; in order to cause the committing of any offence; intending to outrage the modesty of that person; that person is below 14 years of age; in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence against that person under section 354; voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person wrongful restraint; in a lift in any building
